WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.374
"Let's go outside and watch Maggie's riding lesson," Henry suggested.

2
00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:10.487
"Someone might do something suspicious."

3
00:00:10.488 --> 00:00:16.723
"Okay. Maybe you should bring Maggie's sandals so they don't get stolen," Cole said.

4
00:00:16.724 --> 00:00:22.375
Henry was pretty sure Cole was joking. But he picked up the sandals anyway.

5
00:00:22.376 --> 00:00:25.720
"That's a good idea," he said.

6
00:00:25.721 --> 00:00:30.881
"If these sandals disappear, Maggie's parents will freak out."

7
00:00:30.882 --> 00:00:35.402
Cole nodded. "I think Maggie said the riding ring is this way."

8
00:00:35.403 --> 00:00:39.883
He headed toward the back door.

9
00:00:39.884 --> 00:00:43.333
On their way out, the boys passed Jill.

10
00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:46.690
She was trying to yank a wheelbarrow out of a stall.

11
00:00:46.691 --> 00:00:49.588
It was piled high with horse manure.

12
00:00:49.589 --> 00:00:54.951
"Ugh!" Jill cried as the wheelbarrow almost tipped over.

13
00:00:54.952 --> 00:01:01.501
Then she spotted the boys. "Hey," she said. "Will you two help me?

14
00:01:01.502 --> 00:01:03.714
My wheelbarrow is stuck."

15
00:01:03.715 --> 00:01:10.069
"Sure." Henry put down the sandals. Then he and Cole grabbed the wheelbarrow.

16
00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:13.733
Working together, they soon pulled it into the aisle.

17
00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:18.864
"Whew! Thanks." Jill wiped sweat off her forehead.

18
00:01:18.865 --> 00:01:21.857
"I thought I'd never get it out of there."

19
00:01:21.858 --> 00:01:26.460
"Cleaning all these stalls must be hard work," Henry said.

20
00:01:26.461 --> 00:01:32.421
"It is." Jill frowned. "And Ms. Wood doesn't pay me very much."

21
00:01:32.422 --> 00:01:35.439
"So why do you do it?" Cole asked.

22
00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.602
"Because it's the only way to pay for extra riding lessons."

23
00:01:39.603 --> 00:01:45.261
Jill sighed. "I wish I had a way to earn more cash!

24
00:01:45.262 --> 00:01:50.505
Then I could ride every day and not have to clean a bunch of stinky stalls first."

25
00:01:50.506 --> 00:02:00.301
Henry and Cole said good-bye to Jill and headed outdoors.

26
00:02:00.302 --> 00:02:02.951
"Are you thinking what I'm thinking?"

27
00:02:02.952 --> 00:02:07.306
Cole asked as they sat down on a bench outside the riding ring.

28
00:02:07.307 --> 00:02:11.425
"Yes, if you're thinking that Jill should be a suspect."

29
00:02:11.426 --> 00:02:14.485
Henry put Maggie's sandals on the bench.

30
00:02:14.486 --> 00:02:19.353
"It sounds like she'd do anything to get more money for riding."

31
00:02:19.354 --> 00:02:22.861
"Including steal stuff?" Cole asked.

32
00:02:22.862 --> 00:02:25.837
"Who knows?" Henry said.

33
00:02:25.838 --> 00:02:30.096
"She could probably sell Maggie's gloves and charm bracelet.

34
00:02:30.097 --> 00:02:33.579
And she might have thought she could cash that check."

35
00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:37.518
"Okay, we'll put her on the suspect list," Cole said.

36
00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:41.426
"But we'd better not let her know she's on there.

37
00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:45.841
If she turns out to be innocent again, she'll be really annoyed!"

38
00:02:45.842 --> 00:02:47.728
Henry laughed.

39
00:02:47.729 --> 00:02:53.196
The Lemonade Detectives had suspected Jill of stealing during their very first mystery.

40
00:02:53.197 --> 00:02:56.186
She'd turned out to be innocent in that case.

41
00:02:56.187 --> 00:02:59.630
But that didn't mean she was innocent now too.

42
00:02:59.631 --> 00:03:05.388
Henry glanced at the riding ring. "We should be watching our other suspects."

43
00:03:05.389 --> 00:03:08.536
He and Cole watched the lesson for a while.

44
00:03:08.537 --> 00:03:13.169
Ms. Wood stood in the middle of the ring and told the riders what to do.

45
00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:17.719
First she had them walk their horses around in a big circle.

46
00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:20.086
Then she told them to trot.

47
00:03:20.087 --> 00:03:24.857
Henry noticed that trotting was faster, and it looked kind of bouncy.

48
00:03:24.858 --> 00:03:29.070
"This is no fun!" Zach complained loudly.

49
00:03:29.071 --> 00:03:33.031
"Every time my pony trots, I almost fall off."

50
00:03:33.032 --> 00:03:38.007
"That kid really doesn't want to be here, does he?" Cole whispered.

51
00:03:38.008 --> 00:03:43.503
"It's easy, Zach!" Daisy called out. "Just watch me."

52
00:03:43.504 --> 00:03:48.414
As Daisy trotted past the others, Eleanor's pony slowed to a walk.

53
00:03:48.415 --> 00:03:53.872
"Ms. Wood, my pony is lazy!" Eleanor called out.

54
00:03:53.873 --> 00:03:59.048
"I have to squeeze him so often, my leg muscles are tired!"

55
00:03:59.049 --> 00:04:02.703
"You're doing fine, Eleanor," Ms. Wood said.

56
00:04:02.704 --> 00:04:06.285
"Daisy, please come back and join the others."

57
00:04:06.286 --> 00:04:10.733
"But I was just showing Zach how to trot," Daisy said.

58
00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:13.513
"I was doing it right, wasn't I?"

59
00:04:13.514 --> 00:04:17.733
"Daisy is pretty competitive," Cole whispered to Henry.

60
00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:20.599
"She tried out for the swim team, remember?"

61
00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:26.608
Henry nodded. "Maybe she's afraid Maggie is a better rider.

62
00:04:26.609 --> 00:04:31.998
Daisy could be taking Maggie's stuff so Maggie will get in trouble and have to quit."

63
00:04:31.999 --> 00:04:37.815
"Zach has a good motive too," Cole said. "He hates this place.

64
00:04:37.816 --> 00:04:41.220
Maybe he's stealing stuff just to cause trouble."

65
00:04:41.221 --> 00:04:46.333
"Or he could be trying to get his sister in trouble," Henry said.

66
00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:51.442
"If she gets fired, his parents probably wouldn't make him ride anymore."

67
00:04:51.443 --> 00:04:53.964
Cole looked out at the ring again.

68
00:04:53.965 --> 00:04:58.277
Eleanor was still whining about her pony being too slow.

69
00:04:58.278 --> 00:05:00.991
"What about Eleanor?" he said.

70
00:05:00.992 --> 00:05:04.766
"She's the only one who doesn't seem to have a motive.

71
00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:10.735
Maybe she thought that jingling Maggie's charm bracelet at her pony would make him go faster."

72
00:05:10.736 --> 00:05:15.650
Henry laughed. "I doubt that.

73
00:05:15.651 --> 00:05:19.814
We don't know Eleanor very well," he reminded Cole.

74
00:05:19.815 --> 00:05:23.938
"Maybe she has a motive that we haven't figured out yet."

75
00:05:23.939 --> 00:05:29.867
Cole nodded. "All we know is that she's kind of lazy and she has a dog."

76
00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:32.984
"Speaking of her dog, there he is."

77
00:05:32.985 --> 00:05:36.084
Henry saw Little Spot wandering toward them.

78
00:05:36.085 --> 00:05:39.334
The dog stopped to sniff at something on the ground.

79
00:05:39.335 --> 00:05:41.770
Then he came toward them.

80
00:05:41.771 --> 00:05:45.667
"Here, Little Spot." Cole held out his hand.

81
00:05:45.668 --> 00:05:51.308
Little Spot ignored him. He grabbed one of Maggie's sandals and took off!

82
00:05:51.309 --> 00:05:53.886
"Hey!" Henry cried.

83
00:05:53.887 --> 00:06:02.153
"Aha!" Cole said. "I think we just caught the thief!"

